@startuml
title Slow run — the send call fails, the run still lands (correctness never depends on the send)
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

participant "Gateway TeamsRuntime" as GW #C8E6DC
participant "Sweeper\n(5 s ticker)" as Sweep #C8E6DC
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "Agent-Teams env v3\n(validator)" as Chain #FFE4A6
participant "Platform channel" as Platform #F8CECC

group The send fails indeterminately
GW -> API : POST run-under-grant/send (bounded 130 s)
API -> Chain : deploy
alt client timeout fires
GW -> GW : outcome INDETERMINATE: the deploy\nmay have landed; run record STAYS ACTIVE
else embers answers 504 deploy_not_finalized
API --> GW : 504 {code: deploy_not_finalized,\n"poll the run state"}
GW -> GW : same treatment: indeterminate,\nrun stays active
else chain refused the deploy itself
API --> GW : 403 grant_revoked / 429 grant_caps_exceeded /\n402 deploy_unfunded
GW -> GW : nothing registered: evict cached grant,\ndeactivate the record, tell the user
end
end

group Recovery loop: the sweeper polls every active run
loop each 5 s tick, per active run, budget 15 min
Sweep -> API : GET /runs/{run_id}
alt run not yet visible
API --> Sweep : 404 -- keep waiting\n(deploy still finalizing, or lost)
else suspended with waits
API --> Sweep : status suspended, wait_ids, revision
Sweep -> Platform : announce waits ONCE per revision\n(announced_wait_revision fence)
else completed
API --> Sweep : status completed, output hashes
Sweep -> API : reveal prepare + send (grantee authority)
API --> Sweep : 200 output JSON
Sweep -> Platform : **Final**: output + "Run: <url>"
else completed but hashes not yet visible
API --> Sweep : completed, hashes absent (observer lag)
Sweep -> Sweep : stay active; next sweep reveals
else failed / cancelled
API --> Sweep : terminal failure state
Sweep -> Platform : TeamRunFailed (status + last event)
end
end
end

group Budget exhaustion (15 min)
Sweep -> Sweep : deactivate record ("budget_exceeded")
Sweep -> Platform : "Run #N is still not finished after Ns.\nIt may yet complete -- team status #N."
note right of Sweep #FFF0C7
Eviction stops the sweeper, not the run:
"team status #N" still reads the ledger, and
the run completes for its owner regardless.
end note
end

note over GW, Chain #FFF0C7
The f1r3sky lesson, generalized: the blocking send is an
optimization. Every outcome is reachable from
GET /runs/{run_id} plus a grantee reveal, so a dropped
connection, a restart, or a 504 loses nothing. A resent
same-signed envelope carries the same deploy identity and
re-registers idempotently without a second cap unit.
end note
@enduml
